course: dictionary
lesson: 2324
title: Crouch: low and ready
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe a movement you can act out, and crouch is one of them. Picture your own body: bend your knees, lower yourself towards the ground and lean forward a little. That is crouching. «Crouch low, and roll when you fall instead of slamming down a stiff arm.» The words low and roll are clues that crouch means getting down low.
explain: Crouch can be a verb or a noun. As a verb it changes: crouch, crouches, crouched, crouching. As a noun, a crouch is that low, bent position. Look at the words around it to see which one it is: «Watch a cat with a toy mouse: it crouches low» shows the verb, because the cat is doing the action.
explain: Crouch often means getting ready. «Falling from a crouch is a shorter drop than from standing» tells you that a crouch is a low place to start from. Sprinters crouch at the start of a race, ready to spring forward. Crouch does not mean lying flat.
explain: Crouching can keep you safe. In a fire, crouch low, because smoke rises. In an earthquake, crouch under a sturdy table and hold on. These are real safety skills, so knowing this word could help you one day.
fact: Crouch means to bend your knees and lower your body close to the ground, leaning forward a little.
fact: A crouch (noun) is that low, bent position.
fact: Crouch is a verb: crouch, crouches, crouched, crouching.
fact: Phrases like «crouch down», «crouch behind» and «in a crouch» are common.
fact: In a fire, crouch low, because smoke rises.
exercise: «Crouch low, and roll when you fall instead of slamming down a stiff arm.» What does crouch mean here? | To jump high into the air | To run very fast in a circle | To lie flat on your back | *To bend your knees and lower your body close to the ground
exercise: Sprinters crouch at the start of a race. What is a crouch? | A tall, straight stand with arms up | A sleeping position | *A low, bent position, ready to spring forward | A kind of running shoe
exercise: «Watch a cat with a toy mouse: it crouches low, then it shoots forward in one quick pounce.» Find and copy the word that shows what the cat does before it pounces. | mouse | *crouches | pounce | toy
test: In a fire, why should you crouch low? | *Because smoke rises, so the air is cleaner near the floor | Because smoke sinks, so you should stand tall | Because crouching makes you run faster | Because fire likes low places
test: «Crouch to a child's or a pet's eye level» when taking a photo. What does this mean? | Lie flat on the ground with the camera | Stand on a chair to take the photo | Zoom in very close from far away | *Bend down so your eyes are at the same height as theirs
exam: Which sentence uses crouch as a noun? | *In a crouch, the goalkeeper waited for the penalty | The goalkeeper is crouching by the post | The goalkeeper will crouch ready to dive | The goalkeeper crouched low before the penalty
